{
  "title": "3.3.0: Exercises",
  "originalText": "Exercise \\(\\PageIndex{1}\\)\n\nWhich operations have the lowest precedence in order of operations?\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{2}\\)\n\nIf many operations have the same precedence in an expression, in what order should the operations be performed?\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{3}\\)\n\nWhich operations have the same precedence in order of operations?\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{4}\\)\n\nAfter all operations in parentheses have been performed, which operations should be performed next? For the following exercises, perform the indicated calculation.\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{5}\\)\n\n\\(4-5 \\times 6\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{6}\\)\n\n\\(34-10 \\times 6\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{7}\\)\n\n\\(18+8 \\times 13\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{8}\\)\n\n\\(40+12 \\times 17\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{9}\\)\n\n\\(50 \\div 2+8\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{10}\\)\n\n\\(72 \\div 6+18\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{11}\\)\n\n\\(13+4 \\times 3^2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{12}\\)\n\n\\(45-6 \\times 7^3\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{13}\\)\n\n\\(6^2 \\times 5-13 \\times 9^2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{14}\\)\n\n\\(14^2 \\times 8-5 \\times 2^4\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{15}\\)\n\n\\(450 \\div 3^2-56 \\div 2^2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{16}\\)\n\n\\(1,000 \\div 5^3-7 \\times 8^4\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{17}\\)\n\n\\(38 \\times 6-4+5 \\times 18 \\div 10\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{18}\\)\n\n\\(15 \\times 7+23-6 \\times 40 \\div 24\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{19}\\)\n\n\\(600 \\div 12 \\times 5+40-6^2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{20}\\)\n\n\\(2 \\times 12^3 \\div 8 \\times 3-4^5\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{21}\\)\n\n\\(10 \\times 6^3 \\div 2 \\times 5+3^2-240 \\div 8 \\times 9\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{22}\\)\n\n\\(45 \\div 15 \\times 6+7^2-4 \\times 15 \\times 18 \\div 12 \\times 3\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{23}\\)\n\n\\((4+3) \\times 2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{24}\\)\n\n\\(6 \\times(12+8)\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{25}\\)\n\n\\((14-25) \\times 2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{26}\\)\n\n\\((86-61) \\div 5\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{27}\\)\n\n\\((3+2)^3\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{28}\\)\n\n\\((17-12)^4\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{29}\\)\n\n\\((45-60)^2\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{30}\\)\n\n\\((90-101)^3\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{31}\\)\n\n\\((3 \\times 4)^3 \\div 8+5\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{32}\\)\n\n\\((6-9)^2 \\times 5-4\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{33}\\)\n\n\\(4-(6+3) \\times 5+11\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{34}\\)\n\n\\(12+(13-6) \\times 8-130\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{35}\\)\n\n\\(15 \\times(4-1)^2+5 \\times(17+2 \\times 3)+4\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{36}\\)\n\n\\(18 \\times(12-6)^4-8 \\times(30-14 \\times 16)-90\\)\n\nExercise \\(\\PageIndex{37}\\)\n\n\\(4 \\times(5+2 \\times(6+8))+10 \\times 3^2\\)\n\n3.3.0: Exercises is shared under a not declared    license and was authored, remixed, and/or curated by LibreTexts.",
